# R10 live probe — uppercase vs lowercase vs mixed-case country codes
site 38
CONTROL uppercase US
    PUT /api/sites/38/config              -> 200 {"success":true,"message":"Site configuration updated successfully","config":{"id":"f5ebc442d31a","siteId":38,"type":"web","public":true,"embedEnabled":false,"saltUserIds":false,"domain":"tcref-r10-93…
    (waited 10427 ms for the R1 sitesAccessCache window before the read-back)
CONTROL read back
    GET /api/sites/38/excluded-countries  -> 200 {"success":true,"excludedCountries":["US"]}

PROBE lowercase us
    PUT /api/sites/38/config
      -> 400 {"success":false,"error":"Invalid request data","details":{"formErrors":[],"fieldErrors":{"excludedCountries":["Country code must be a 2-letter ISO code (e.g., US, GB, CN)"]}}}

PROBE mixed-case Us
    PUT /api/sites/38/config
      -> 400 {"success":false,"error":"Invalid request data","details":{"formErrors":[],"fieldErrors":{"excludedCountries":["Country code must be a 2-letter ISO code (e.g., US, GB, CN)"]}}}

read back after the refusals
    GET /api/sites/38/excluded-countries  -> 200 {"success":true,"excludedCountries":["US"]}

